WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.367
An election

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:00.633
where there's

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.302
no polling, there's only one frontrunner,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.070
but where it all could come unglued

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.771
for that frontrunner

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.705
of just a handful of votes

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.040
go the other way.

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.541
In a nutshell is House

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.376
Minority Leader Kevin

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.877
McCarthy existence right now?

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:12.712
He wants to be desperately the next House

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.880
speaker in the upcoming

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.148
new Republican controlled House.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.384
But because his new majority is so slim,

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.051
as you know, he's

00:00:18.051 --> 00:00:19.319
got to keep as many hardliners

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.087
as possible from voting no.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:22.856
As some have already vowed to do.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.923
So he's also got to keep

00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:24.791
moderates on board

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:28.361
and not end up a hostage to the extreme

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:29.763
supporters of the former president

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.731
if he actually gets the job,

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.600
but also not Eliot them

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.101
completely, which might explain

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:37.203
some of his recent verbal contortions,

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.371
such as condemning the former

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.039
president's dinner

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:39.873
with anti-Semite

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:40.807
but without actually

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.342
condemning the host by name.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:44.377
I don't

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:45.445
think anybody should

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.713
be spending any time

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.580
with Nick Fletcher's.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.749
He has no place in this Republican Party.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:51.885
I think President Trump

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.654
came out four times and condemned him

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.023
and didn't know who he was.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.324
Just as a point of fact,

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.794
the former president has never condemned

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:02.562
that person, let alone four times

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:03.196
in any event.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:04.097
Congressman McCarthy's

00:01:04.097 --> 00:01:05.432
zigzagging is not exactly new.

00:01:05.432 --> 00:01:06.399
Here he is shortly

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.435
after the January six attack on Congress

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.105
The president bears responsibility

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:12.872
for Wednesday's

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:15.041
attack on Congress by mob rioters.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:16.943
He should have immediately

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:18.278
denounced the mob

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:20.647
when he saw what was unfolding.

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:22.916
These facts require immediate action

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:24.884
by President Trump.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:25.652
I was just days

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.253
after the insurrection, famously

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:27.987
not long after

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.122
he was back in Mar

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:29.823
a Lago

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:32.192
currying favor with his supporters.

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.460
Since Entourage

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.594
joins us now with more on his belt

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.495
latest balancing act.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.063
So as of tonight,

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.031
how does McCarthy's

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:40.066
path to the speakership?

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.368
How does it look like he'll get there?

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.503
It's really uncertain

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.471
at this point, Anderson.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:46.272
And this is precisely the concern

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.740
that McCarthy and his allies

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.342
had in the run up to the midterms.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.910
They spent a ton of money

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.511
to try to build

00:01:51.511 --> 00:01:53.313
what they call the governing majority.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.314
They wanted to.

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:54.914
30 seats,

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.817
235 seats, maybe even 240 seats.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:01:58.818
They got probably

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:00.887
were looking at 222 seats.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:02.355
And that means to get become

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.223
elected speaker,

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.292
he'd have 218 votes on January 3rd.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.728
So if for more than four Republicans

00:02:08.728 --> 00:02:09.863
vote against him, vote

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:10.930
for another candidate,

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.866
that means he will have a problem.

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:13.566
And right now

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.435
there are about five Republicans

00:02:15.435 --> 00:02:16.936
hardliners who are signaling

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:18.872
they will either are either nosed

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:19.873
or that they're very likely

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:20.974
to vote against him,

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.108
meaning that McCarthy at

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.877
the moment has a math problem.

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.512
Now talking to some of those hardliners,

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.213
they tell me that there's more than five.

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.248
They say there could be 20.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.116
They're even larger number than that.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:30.683
And some of them,

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:31.551
like Congressman Bob

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:32.819
Good of Virginia, told me

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:34.454
he is urging more to come out

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:35.989
publicly and make clear

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.457
that McCarthy does not have the votes

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.491
say they are opposed.

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.392
And at that point,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.994
he says that there will be another

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.462
candidate who will emerge

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:45.798
There's a

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.933
quality candidates

00:02:46.933 --> 00:02:48.902
who represent the conservative center

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.236
of the Republican conference

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.472
who are privately acknowledging that once

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:52.906
it becomes

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.207
clear it's not going to Kevin McCarthy,

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.642
they are interested in becoming speaker,

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:57.043
but they're not going to raise their hand

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:59.379
publicly until it's clear to them

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.747
that it's not going to be Kevin McCarthy.

00:03:00.747 --> 00:03:01.948
Are you one of these private

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:02.448
no votes

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:04.083
that McCarthy is not coming up publicly

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:04.784
to say so?

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.286
That my position is pretty clear on this

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:08.621
is that no one is telling sort of 18.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.722
And the whole point here

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:10.523
is to have a conversation.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.958
Now, I'm not talking about

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.959
how I'm going to vote or not vote

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:14.460
what I'm talking about is

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.595
my constituents

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:17.864
sent me here to end the status quo.

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:19.732
So, Chip Roy, that

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:20.833
last congressman is

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.435
what gives McCarthy and his allies

00:03:22.435 --> 00:03:22.835
some hope.

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.270
They believe they can win over

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.239
some of those detractors of critics

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:27.807
by negotiating with them.

00:03:27.807 --> 00:03:28.441
And McCarthy

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:30.176
did get a boost from more mainstream

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:31.444
Republicans earlier today.

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.780
The letter was sent from 21 Republicans

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.915
warning about dire consequences

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:36.749
with a massive floor

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:37.717
fight on the first day

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:38.551
of the new Congress,

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:39.385
saying in the letter,

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.253
make no mistake,

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:41.554
we will not allow this conference

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:42.989
to be dragged down a path

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:44.357
to a paralyzed house

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.993
that weakens our hard fought majority,

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.928
showing real signs of tension

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.196
even before they take the majority

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.030
next year Anderson.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:51.297
I mean,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.400
is there anyone who could actually make

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:55.535
a run at the speakership

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.971
if he doesn't get the 218 votes?

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.205
That's also unclear.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:03:59.872
What we have learned

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:02.108
is that Republicans in this hard

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:02.542
line group

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.409
have reached out

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.445
to some of McCarthy's own top deputies,

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.613
including Steve Scalise,

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:07.914
the number two Republican,

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:08.881
and also Tom Emmer,

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.515
who is going to be the number

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:10.316
three Republican

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:11.384
in the new Congress,

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:11.918
as well as Jim

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.186
Jordan is expected to be the House

00:04:13.186 --> 00:04:14.387
Judiciary Committee chairman.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.755
They asked all of them

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.156
to jump into this race.

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.424
We were told that all of them said

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.460
no, that they are backing McCarthy.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.961
Now, the hope among these

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:22.161
these

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.563
the McCarthy detractors,

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:25.965
is that once it is abundantly clear

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.634
he cannot become elected speaker,

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:29.702
somebody else could jump into this race.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.938
Perhaps one of those three At the moment,

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:32.538
they're not signaling

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:33.573
they will do just that.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.140
But, Anderson,

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.009
this is such a rare scenario

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:36.776
that we are talking about.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:38.611
If he cannot get 218 votes,

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.079
McCarthy on January 3rd,

00:04:40.079 --> 00:04:41.447
then we'll go to a second ballot

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:41.881
of voting

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.549
and third ballot of voting potentially

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:45.985
even beyond. It's been 100 years.

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:47.987
1923 was the last time

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.455
there have been more than one ballot

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.591
to elect House Speaker as possible.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.558
That could happen again.

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:53.726
Now on with Roger.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:54.627
Thanks so much. Appreciate it.

